1.) CLIENT - SERVER MODEL :  

The web is a service that allows computers to share and exchange data
The web  is reffered to as client - server model
where the computer that asks for data - client .. and computer that recieves the data - server

The Client : 
The devices the end user uses to acces the data

The Client Program : 
Program that allows users to make request , eg : Web Browser..etc

so, InShort 
A CLient , whether it is a machine or a program , is an appliance and a way to make requests through the web.

The Server : 
It is a computer program 
It contains web resources, host web applications, stores users data.. etc
It is used  to store hundreds or thousands of clients
A Server is always listening for requests, as soon as it hears one , it responds.


Types of servers : 
1.Web Servers - Serve HTTP Request
2.Databse Servers - Server SQL Requests

